            <ArticleTitle>Antisecretory agents in gastrointestinal obstruction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>327-34</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Gastrointestinal obstruction is associated with nausea, vomiting, and abdominal pain. Antisecretory agents can relieve these symptoms, even in the absence of surgical or mechanical intervention. These medical management approaches are outlined, and recommendations are made.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
